<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">William Lyon Mackenzie</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1795">1795</a>–<a href="/years/1861">1861</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">William <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lyon">Lyon</a> Mackenzie was a Scottish-born journalist and politician in Upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a>, a radical critic of the ruling Family Compact and the first mayor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toronto">Toronto</a> in 1834. In December 1837 he led a short-lived armed rebellion near Toronto, which was quickly defeated. He fled to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, where he set up a provisional government on Navy Island, and returned to Canada after an amnesty in 1849.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/william-lyon-mackenzie.jpg" alt="William Lyon Mackenzie" width="320" height="400" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:WilliamLyonMackenzie.jpeg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
